{%- comment -%}
  Launch dates — one source for the card badge and the product page label.

  Accepts:
  - product  {Object}  required
  - variant  {Object}  optional. With it, the date for that edition. Without it, the EARLIEST
                       upcoming date for the product — which is what a card should say.

  Echoes the translated line ("Available from November 10th") while the date is in the future, and
  nothing at all once it passes — so a label takes itself down on launch day and nobody has to
  remember. Never guess a date: a product with no confirmed date simply has no row here, and the
  caller falls back to "Coming soon".

  Rows: handle | option value or * | YYYYMMDD | locale key
  The words live in locales (walterin.launch.*) so they translate; the date lives here so the
  expiry is one comparison. **When a metafield definition is next created in admin, this table
  should move to a product metafield** — content does not belong in code. Until then this is the
  single place it lives, which is the important part.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign rows = 'tarot|*|20261110|walterin.launch.nov10,walterin-prague|Digital Interactive Edition|20261023|walterin.launch.oct23,walterin-prague|Printed Collector’s Edition|20261110|walterin.launch.nov10' | split: ','
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
  assign best_date = 0
  assign best_key = ''

  for row in rows
    assign f = row | split: '|'
    assign r_handle = f[0]
    assign r_value = f[1]
    assign r_date = f[2] | plus: 0
    assign r_key = f[3]

    if r_handle != product.handle
      continue
    endif
    if r_date <= today
      continue
    endif
    if variant != blank and r_value != '*'
      unless variant.options contains r_value
        continue
      endunless
    endif

    if best_date == 0 or r_date < best_date
      assign best_date = r_date
      assign best_key = r_key
    endif
  endfor

  if best_key != blank
    echo best_key | t
  endif
-%}
